--- SAT proofs (yosys) --------------------------------------
  fv_enc_disparity       encoder never emits an illegal disparity
      PROVED (unsat: no input makes the property fail)
  fv_enc_rd_tracking     reported running disparity matches the symbol
      PROVED (unsat: no input makes the property fail)
  fv_comma_format        K28.5 encodings match the vendor comma constants
      PROVED (unsat: no input makes the property fail)
  fv_injective           encoding is injective (decode table well defined)
      PROVED (unsat: no input makes the property fail)
  fv_run_length          no run of more than five identical bits on the wire
      PROVED (unsat: no input makes the property fail)

--- exhaustive enumeration (icarus) -------------------------
  the decode table is a procedurally initialised memory, which SAT
  cannot take. Its input space is small enough to enumerate in full,
  which is an equally complete argument.


